From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Wed, 23 Sep 2026 22:03:10 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 003/260] [ae-patch] Add an item-observers registry the server
 calls after it persists harness items

Phase 4 of omnigent-ae (patch P3, 2026-09-23). The branch-discipline layer
needs to read what the assistant wrote (a `FORK:` gate, an `Absorbed:`
marker, a handoff note) and set session labels from it, and nothing in
upstream exposes that moment: a native Claude Code session's turns arrive
as `external_conversation_item` events that never reach the `response`
policy phase, and a runner-relayed harness's text is persisted at the
relay's flush, where a `response`-phase ASK behaves as a DENY. So the
capture is an observer, never a policy.

New `omnigent/server/item_observers.py`: `register_item_observer(fn)`,
`unregister_item_observer(fn)`, `notify_items_persisted(session_id, items)`
and `drain_item_observers()` for tests. Notification is fire-and-forget:
each observer runs as a task on the running loop (a sync observer on a
worker thread, so store I/O never blocks the loop), and whatever it raises
is logged and dropped. Registration is idempotent so a module that
registers at import survives a re-import. The registry is process-local
like `omnigent.runtime.session_stream` and empty until something registers,
so an unpatched-looking server behaves exactly as before.

Two call sites, two lines each (the import and the call):
`_persist_external_conversation_item` in
`omnigent/server/routes/_sessions/orchestration.py` after the append and
the dedupe early return, so a re-posted item notifies nobody; and
`_flush_relay_text` in `omnigent/server/routes/_sessions/helpers.py` after
the assistant segment is confirmed persisted. The legacy
`external_assistant_message` event has no live producer and is left alone.

Tests: `tests/server/test_item_observers.py` covers the registry (sync and
async observers, idempotent registration, a failing observer logged while
the others still run, a sync observer proven off the loop, the no-loop
warning), the bridge through the real app (`external_conversation_item`
via the `client` fixture, a deduplicated re-post, a failing observer that
still lets the item persist) and the relay flush against the stub store
`test_relay_output_policy_deny.py` uses.

